// #2263: a `Map[Double, V]` annotation must not hand `Array[String]` keys to
// String ops. Two rules now stand behind that, and this fixture pins the
// OUTER one: a `Double` key is not one the builtin map takes, so the
// annotation itself is rejected where it is written, and the body below is
// never reached.
//
// The inner rule -- `Map::keys` answering with the receiver's KEY slot rather
// than a fixed `Array[String]` (#2272) -- is what types the keys of an
// `Int`-keyed map as `Array[Int]` (#2334).
fn f(m: Map[Float64, String]) -> Int {
  let ks = Map::keys(m)
  String::length(Array::get(ks, 0))
}
fn main {
  ()
}
